# Athlete-OS Recomp Rules

## Subject Profile
- 32yo male BJJ brown belt (turning 33 Jan 20, 2027)
- Height: 5'5" (165.1 cm)
- Guatemalan descent (high prevalence of SLC16A11, LCT-13910 CC lactase non-persistence, ABCA1 R230C)

## Transformation Trajectory (147 Days / 21 Weeks)

### Baseline (Week 0 - Nov 6, 2026)
- Scale weight: 189.7 lbs (86.05 kg)
- Body fat: 26.1–27.0% BF (49.5–51.2 lbs FM)
- Lean body mass: 138.5–140.2 lbs LBM
- Navel waist: 36.0"
- Pants: tight size 34
- Gi: standard A1 gi gaps by 1.5" at navel

### Target (Week 21 - Apr 2, 2027)
- Scale weight: 172.0 lbs (range 170–174 lbs)
- Body fat: 14.9% BF (25.6 lbs FM; −23.9 lbs pure fat)
- Lean body mass: 146.4 lbs LBM (+6.2 lbs net LBM: +8.2 lbs gross muscle/glycogen/ICW offset by −2.0 lbs ECW/gut residue)
- Navel waist: 31.5" (range 31–32")
- Pants: size 31–32
- Gi: standard A1 gi ≥5.5" lapel overlap (2026 IBJJF legal: ≤2 cm wrist/ankle gap, ≥7 cm sleeve opening, 20–30 cm belt tails)

## Energetics Model
- Baseline BMR: 1,737 kcal (Mifflin-St Jeor) / 1,727 kcal (Katch-McArdle)
- Baseline TDEE: 2,875–2,920 kcal/day (NEAT ~480 kcal @ 8.5k–10k steps, TEF ~265 kcal, EAT ~478 kcal)
- By Week 21: Mifflin-St Jeor BMR drops to 1,657 kcal, but Katch-McArdle BMR rises to 1,791 kcal (+64 kcal/day) due to +6.2 lbs LBM expansion, supporting a 2,500 kcal permanent maintenance floor

## Critical Diagnostic Rule (Weeks 1–3 ICW Buffer)
During Weeks 1–3, 5g/day creatine and myonuclear domain re-inflation pull +3.8 lbs of intracellular water and glycogen into muscle cells. Scale weight may hover at 187.5–188.5 lbs for the first 14–21 days despite fat loss. **NEVER cut calories during Weeks 1–3 if navel waist is tightening.**

## Hard Guardrails
- Zero GLP-1 agonists
- Enforce ≥100g protein (target 110–125g) before 5:00 PM daily
- Enforce pre-meal unflavored psyllium husk (2.5g Adaptation in Wk 1; 5.0g Operational in Wks 2–21) in 12 oz water + 6 oz chaser 15–20 min before Lunch and Dinner (never within 2 hrs of BJJ)
- Derive 65–75% of non-peri-workout carbs from Milpa resistant starches (cooked black/pinto beans, nixtamalized corn tortillas)

